  "notes": "{疑|うたが}う is a transitive godan verb meaning to doubt, question, or suspect.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive) - takes ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ for the object of doubt.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{疑|うたが}う: to doubt one's eyes (can't believe what you see)\n- ⟦{耳|みみ}→耳：01513_mimi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{疑|うたが}う: to doubt one's ears (can't believe what you hear)\n- ⟦{疑|うたが}い→疑い：09757_utagai⟧なく: without doubt, undoubtedly\n- ⟦{疑|うたが}い→疑い：09757_utagai⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦かける→かける：00854_kakeru⟧: to cast suspicion on\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{疑|うたが}い→疑い：09757_utagai⟧: doubt, suspicion (noun)\n- ⟦{疑問|ぎもん}→疑問：02648_gimon⟧: question, doubt\n- ⟦{疑惑|ぎわく}→疑惑：13602_giwaku⟧: suspicion, distrust\n- ⟦{半信半疑|はんしんはんぎ}→半信半疑：20643_hanshinhangi⟧: half in doubt\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {疑|うたが}っている: suspects, doubts (stative — describes a current mental attitude, not an action)\n- Note: Like ⟦{信|しん}じる→信じる：01111_shinjiru⟧ and ⟦{思|おも}う→思う：00492_omou⟧, {疑|うたが}う in the ている form expresses a sustained mental stance. ⟦{警察|けいさつ}→警察：01393_keisatsu⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧⟦{彼|かれ}→彼：01292_kare⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{疑|うたが}っている = 'the police suspect him.' The plain form usually refers to the moment of forming the doubt or is used in literary writing.",
